---
import { DiffDemo } from '../components/DiffDemo';
import '../styles/site.css';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>hihyou (批評) — an alternative GitHub code review experience</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A browser extension that takes over the GitHub PR changes view: hunk-level seen state, AST-aware picking, moved-code detection, TS hover, and more."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <h1><span class="kanji">批評</span> hihyou</h1>
        <p class="tagline">
          An alternative GitHub code review experience — a browser extension
          that takes over the PR "changes" view in place and rebuilds it
          around actually applying the review.
        </p>
      </section>

      <ul class="features">
        <li>
          <h3>Viewer takeover</h3>
          <p>
            Renders every file's diff itself from GitHub's own route payload;
            the PR header and tabs stay native, and a floating 批評 pill
            toggles back at any time.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Hunk-level seen state</h3>
          <p>
            Drag across lines and press <code>s</code>: seen hunks anchor as
            content hashes and dim. A later commit touching the range
            invalidates them automatically.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Apply hunks locally</h3>
          <p>
            <code>a</code> applies the selection as a git diff to your local
            checkout — entirely in the browser via the File System Access
            API, verified against the file first.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>AST core</h3>
          <p>
            web-tree-sitter in the background worker: scope snapping, sticky
            scope headers, import folding, structural diff, and moved-code
            detection that inherits seen state.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Commit timeline + stacked PRs</h3>
          <p>
            A commit strip with prev/next navigation; stacked PRs flatten
            into one sequence, and commit navigation morphs code with
            shiki-magic-move.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Twoslash TS hover</h3>
          <p>
            Quick-info popovers typed against the exact dependency versions
            in the repo's pnpm-lock at the reviewed commit, with .d.ts pulled
            from npm tarballs.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Rich markdown diff</h3>
          <p>
            .md files render as prose with word-level ins/del tracked
            changes; toggle back to the source diff per file.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Inline review threads</h3>
          <p>
            Existing line-anchored comment threads render under their lines,
            resolved ones collapsed.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <section class="demo-section">
        <h2>Try the viewer</h2>
        <p>
          The real <code>@hihyou/diff-viewer</code> over a captured payload
          (wxt-dev/wxt#2464). Click the tree, fold files, drag-select lines
          and press <code>s</code> to mark them applied.
        </p>
        <div class="demo-frame">
          <DiffDemo client:only="solid-js" />
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
